In general, it's safe to enchant armor when it's at +3 (+4 for elven
stuff). If you use a blessed scroll, it can get boosted as far as +6
in one shot. More often, you'll end up with +4 or +5. If you don't get
enough, you can use a cursed scroll or - carefully - dance with a
disenchanter to knock it down to +3 and try again.

Enchanting after that is iffy, and the odds are very good that you'll
lose the item. It can be done, tho', if you have the scrolls and items
to waste.

Weapons work similarly, but can safely be enchanted one point higher
(safe at +4, +5 for elven weapons).

Both weapons and armor sometimes "vibrate unexpectedly" to warn you
that you're close to blowing 'em up. Sometimes they don't.

